  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One primary journey: cloud Summary",
      "items": [
        "The bright path follows a saved note from Flutter to DeepSeek. UI acceptance occurs only while the selected snapshot and session remain current.",
        "Client-side RemoteSummarizationService chooses one direct call or sequential sections plus one merge; the backend does not orchestrate the whole pipeline.",
        "The shared policy budgets 16,000 estimated input tokens, 128 section / 256 final output tokens, up to four sections + merge. No automatic generation retry; one HTTP token-refresh resend on 401 is separate.",
        "The response returns through the same request path. Backend and client validate it; non-stop / partial provider output is refused."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Trust boundaries and authority",
      "items": [
        "Client gates improve UX but do not establish server authority. HTTP APIs verify Cognito JWTs; Summary also requires an access-token subject and current consent declaration.",
        "Summary Lambda rereads note ownership/access, protection grant and revisions before generation and before accepting the result. The conditional run ledger binds sections and merge inputs.",
        "The DeepSeek key is an Amplify backend secret, resolved inside Lambda. Flutter receives public deployment configuration and Cognito session tokens, never the provider key.",
        "Drawn boundaries express ownership/trust, not VPC security groups. Only authorized Summary content crosses into the external provider."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Local-first state and durable synchronization",
      "items": [
        "Per-account encrypted state uses IndexedDB on Web and app-support files on native platforms. Atomic compare-and-set protects a newer snapshot from stale writers.",
        "Application/domain ports isolate SDK details; the SyncCoordinator owns outbox push/pull and conflict handling. Labels and preferences share the account store.",
        "Sync/security handlers own canonical note transactions, ACL and protected-note operations. Client state is not the source of truth for cloud authorization."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Supporting I/O: attachments and realtime",
      "items": [
        "S3 arrows show backend verification/finalization. Presigned staging PUT capabilities allow direct client uploads; URL and checksum/version steps are abbreviated here.",
        "The attachment bucket is private, TLS-only, versioned and retained. Web uploads require an explicitly allowed HTTPS origin; no bucket access is implied by a diagram arrow.",
        "EVENT# inserts trigger a relay; a one-minute EventBridge rule retries outstanding work. AppSync scopes subscriptions to the authenticated actor and uses IAM publication.",
        "WebSocket payloads are revision hints, not canonical note reads. The client requests HTTP synchronization after receiving them."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Snapshot, alternatives and scope",
      "items": [
        "Source snapshot: final-tuankiet at 6f37931. The original project is the evidence root; the older worktree was not used. Component citations are pinned to committed source.",
        "Remote Summary requires explicit NOTEFLOW_AI_MODE=remote, Cognito and a valid HTTPS endpoint. Blank/local mode instead uses the native local worker; Web local inference is unavailable.",
        "Native local inference remains an optional worker / LocalLlmBridge path (main.dart:971-993). Hosting on Mac mini / Cloudflare and RAG proposals are outside this runtime view.",
        "Graph MCP was unavailable; the local index excludes Dart. Exact source and call sites were inspected. This diagram proves code wiring, not a fresh deployment or live-provider acceptance."
      ]
    }
  ]
